            <ArticleTitle>[Churg-Strauss syndrome (two case reports)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>288-92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Churg-Strauss syndrome is a necrotizing vasculitis with multiple organ involvement characterized by asthma, peripheral blood eosinophilia, eosinophilic tissue infiltration and extravascular granulomas. A 35 years-old male with 6-months history of asthma and a 43 years-old female with 4-years history of asthma, were further examined due to clinical worsening and lesions on chest radiographs. They were finally diagnosed as Churg-Strauss syndrome. Clinical and radiological response to oral corticosteroid therapy was obtained.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
